  "decisions": [
    "Preserve the resumed isolated clone, original134-case handoff fixture, unchanged smoke harness, legacy sealStagingHandoff function and both earlier scaffold baselines.",
    "Separate protocol2 cleanup/smoke-owned purpose and explicit original ownership/renewal selection from protocol1 probe/create-only smoke.",
    "Use only fixed account/origins/issuer/audience/registry context and independently reviewed local/source/deployed context; no caller-selectable tenant, store, destination or command.",
    "Bootstrap is one explicit30m POST plus one exact-ID readback under30-second wall/monotonic decision bounds; capture acknowledged exact UUID before late validation and never delete or adopt by name.",
    "Prepare real RSA/AES before mutations, observe both latest/current Worker bindings, select only the first current deployment with explicit percentage strategy and exactly one100percent active version, and never fall back to history.",
    "Owned sealing permits at most one explicitly selected30m renewal when necessary and one exact original-ID rotation with independent expiry/identity readback; original created_at need not survive mutation.",
    "Never compute protocol2 expiry from created_at plus requested duration. Required optional provider observations fail closed. Attempted and acknowledged writes remain distinct after late, rejected, missing or lost responses.",
    "Anchor observed token lifetime to monotonic receipt time; require strictly more than455000ms after all crypto/source/spawn awaits, with no await before plaintext pipe release.",
    "Cleanup uses only fixed public health, authenticated dashboard and same-origin revoke-all. Require typed acknowledged mutation plus both final checks; final emptiness cannot rescue a lost acknowledgement.",
    "Cleanup has bounded input, per-request30-second/1MiB responses and180-second work budget; parent retains450-second child/5-second close bounds and requires actual natural close.",
    "Independent source review and provider evidence prompted a16-case extension before fixes. Actual RED exposed four failures: valid history handling, missing/unknown current strategy, and a smoke-only marker admitted by cleanup output parsing.",
    "Terminal-newline hypotheses were disproved by actual Node24 execution: all added newline checks already passed as negative controls. No validator behavior was changed for that disproved hypothesis.",
    "Root owns actual provider/connected qualification, shared roadmap review/render, hosted gates and publication. No live provider call, Windows action, remote write or model-consuming command occurred in this worker."
  ],
